   -2020,  "Piano I mean, I know you were probably thinking about that's beautiful. Something about life, but I love music and I wish I had learned the piano when I was young. Do you still play? No no.":



2.1974, "What is something that you used to be sure about but that you now are less sure about?":

   -1990,  "A sense of right and wrong or good and evil. Mhm. When I was young, I had a very strong sense of it. That's a great answer. And now I'm not so sure about what it is. It's a great answer.":



3.1985, "If you could go back and live in any age, where would you like to go and what would you ask?":

   -2020,  "I would go back to the Paleolithic Era and our earliest ancestors because I'm fascinated by their world and what they were like. So the Paleolithic, 20,000 years ago. Okay. And I would like to know about their their religion, their spirituality. I'm interested in the origin of human consciousness.":



4.1995, "If you could have three people over at your dinner party any three people you choose, living or dead, who would they be?":

   -2010,  "Frederick Nietzsche because I'm reading a biography of his right now. That's unbelievable. Um, the other would be Buddha one odd and then the other would be Ulysses.":



5.2003, "If you could have something you're trying to learn right now, what would it be?":

   -2020,  "Something I'm trying to learn right now is forgiveness about myself because I'm extremely unforgiving with myself. Yeah not easy it's not been my life pattern where did the pursuit begin and why is it a worthy Pursuit.":



7
 }
